@namespace DotNetCloud.Modules.About.UI

<div class="help-content">
    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">About DotNetCloud</h2>
        <p>DotNetCloud is a self-hosted, open-source cloud platform built with .NET — a modern alternative to NextCloud. It provides file storage, chat, calendar, contacts, notes, bookmarks, email, photos, music, video, project tracking, and an AI assistant, all running on your own infrastructure.</p>
        <p>The About page is organized into sections, selectable from the sidebar: <strong>Overview</strong>, <strong>Version</strong>, and <strong>Attributions</strong>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Version Information</h2>
        <p>The <strong>Version</strong> section shows the product name, version, file version, .NET runtime, operating system, architecture, and processor count — all read from the running assembly at startup, so they reflect the exact build you are running.</p>
        <p>Each module tracks its own version independently of the core platform. The <strong>Modules</strong> section links to the <strong>Modules</strong> admin page, where you can see individual module versions and statuses.</p>
        <p>Check the <strong>Open-Source Attributions</strong> section for bundled library, NuGet package, and Docker base image licensing information.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">License</h2>
        <p>DotNetCloud is licensed under <strong>AGPL-3.0</strong>. The logo and mascot are <strong>CC BY-ND 4.0</strong>, and the documentation is <strong>CC BY-SA 4.0</strong>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Getting Help</h2>
        <ul class="help-tips">
            <li>Every module has a built-in help page — click the help button at the bottom of the module's sidebar.</li>
            <li>Visit the project repository for documentation and issue tracking.</li>
            <li>Report bugs or request features on GitHub.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
